{"schema_version":2,"id":"p304-brain-waves-classroom","revision":1,"title_en":"Measuring Brain Waves in the Classroom","title_zh":"在课堂中测量脑电波","level":"B2","primary_topic":"technology","tags":["science","neuroscience","technology","education"],"source_type":"licensed_adaptation","fiction":false,"summary_zh":"大脑中的860亿个神经元通过微弱电脉冲进行交流，数千神经元同步放电形成了规律起伏的脑电波。传统实验室脑电图（EEG）利用电极帽检测头皮电信号，但难以捕捉现实社交互动。纽约大学研究人员使用便携式EEG头戴设备对高中生物课进行了前沿观测，发现课堂投入度更高的学生与同学之间展现出更强的脑间电波同步性（brain-to-brain synchrony）。然而，便携式脑电也面临传感器较少、身体运动干扰等权衡，且无法读取具体思想，研究人员特此警惕对专注力分类的商业夸大宣称。","featured":false,"admitted_at":"2026-11-21T12:31:44Z","paragraphs":[{"sentences":[{"id":"s1","text":"Inside your brain, roughly 86 billion nerve cells called neurons are constantly communicating.","separator_after":" ","translation_zh":"在你的大脑内部，大约860亿个被称为神经元的神经细胞正在时刻进行交流。","tokens":[{"start":0,"end":6,"surface":"Inside","lemma":"inside","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"在……内部"},{"start":7,"end":11,"surface":"your","lemma":"your","pos":"代词","gloss_zh":"你的"},{"start":12,"end":17,"surface":"brain","lemma":"brain","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"大脑"},{"start":19,"end":26,"surface":"roughly","lemma":"roughly","pos":"副词","gloss_zh":"大约"},{"start":30,"end":37,"surface":"billion","lemma":"billion","pos":"数词","gloss_zh":"十亿"},{"start":38,"end":43,"surface":"nerve","lemma":"nerve","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"神经"},{"start":44,"end":49,"surface":"cells","lemma":"cell","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"细胞"},{"start":50,"end":56,"surface":"called","lemma":"call","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"被称为"},{"start":57,"end":64,"surface":"neurons","lemma":"neuron","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"神经元"},{"start":65,"end":68,"surface":"are","lemma":"be","pos":"助动词","gloss_zh":"正"},{"start":69,"end":79,"surface":"constantly","lemma":"constantly","pos":"副词","gloss_zh":"不断地"},{"start":80,"end":93,"surface":"communicating","lemma":"communicate","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"交流"}],"phrases":[{"start":38,"end":49,"surface":"nerve cells","gloss_zh":"神经细胞"}]},{"id":"s2","text":"Instead of using words, these cells talk to each other through tiny electrical pulses.","separator_after":" ","translation_zh":"这些细胞并不使用言语，而是通过微小的电脉冲与彼此对话。","tokens":[{"start":0,"end":7,"surface":"Instead","lemma":"instead","pos":"副词","gloss_zh":"代替"},{"start":8,"end":10,"surface":"of","lemma":"of","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"而不是"},{"start":11,"end":16,"surface":"using","lemma":"use","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"使用"},{"start":17,"end":22,"surface":"words","lemma":"word","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"话语"},{"start":24,"end":29,"surface":"these","lemma":"these","pos":"限定词","gloss_zh":"这些"},{"start":30,"end":35,"surface":"cells","lemma":"cell","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"细胞"},{"start":36,"end":40,"surface":"talk","lemma":"talk","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"对话"},{"start":41,"end":43,"surface":"to","lemma":"to","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"向"},{"start":44,"end":48,"surface":"each","lemma":"each","pos":"代词","gloss_zh":"每"},{"start":49,"end":54,"surface":"other","lemma":"other","pos":"代词","gloss_zh":"另一个"},{"start":55,"end":62,"surface":"through","lemma":"through","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"通过"},{"start":63,"end":67,"surface":"tiny","lemma":"tiny","pos":"形容词","gloss_zh":"微小的"},{"start":68,"end":78,"surface":"electrical","lemma":"electrical","pos":"形容词","gloss_zh":"电的"},{"start":79,"end":85,"surface":"pulses","lemma":"pulse","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"脉冲"}],"phrases":[{"start":0,"end":10,"surface":"Instead of","gloss_zh":"而不是；代替"},{"start":36,"end":54,"surface":"talk to each other","gloss_zh":"互相交谈；彼此交流"},{"start":68,"end":85,"surface":"electrical pulses","gloss_zh":"电脉冲"}]},{"id":"s3","text":"When thousands of neighboring neurons fire together, their combined electrical activity rises and falls in rhythmic patterns known as brain waves.","separator_after":"","translation_zh":"当数以千计的相邻神经元一同放电时，它们的综合电活动便会形成规律起伏的节律模式，这就是我们所说的脑电波。","tokens":[{"start":0,"end":4,"surface":"When","lemma":"when","pos":"连词","gloss_zh":"当……时"},{"start":5,"end":14,"surface":"thousands","lemma":"thousand","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"成千上万"},{"start":15,"end":17,"surface":"of","lemma":"of","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"……的"},{"start":18,"end":29,"surface":"neighboring","lemma":"neighboring","pos":"形容词","gloss_zh":"相邻的"},{"start":30,"end":37,"surface":"neurons","lemma":"neuron","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"神经元"},{"start":38,"end":42,"surface":"fire","lemma":"fire","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"放电"},{"start":43,"end":51,"surface":"together","lemma":"together","pos":"副词","gloss_zh":"共同"},{"start":53,"end":58,"surface":"their","lemma":"they","pos":"代词","gloss_zh":"它们的"},{"start":59,"end":67,"surface":"combined","lemma":"combine","pos":"形容词","gloss_zh":"综合的"},{"start":68,"end":78,"surface":"electrical","lemma":"electrical","pos":"形容词","gloss_zh":"电的"},{"start":79,"end":87,"surface":"activity","lemma":"activity","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"活动"},{"start":88,"end":93,"surface":"rises","lemma":"rise","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"上升"},{"start":94,"end":97,"surface":"and","lemma":"and","pos":"连词","gloss_zh":"和"},{"start":98,"end":103,"surface":"falls","lemma":"fall","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"下降"},{"start":104,"end":106,"surface":"in","lemma":"in","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"以……形式"},{"start":107,"end":115,"surface":"rhythmic","lemma":"rhythmic","pos":"形容词","gloss_zh":"有节律的"},{"start":116,"end":124,"surface":"patterns","lemma":"pattern","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"模式"},{"start":125,"end":130,"surface":"known","lemma":"know","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"已知"},{"start":131,"end":133,"surface":"as","lemma":"as","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"作为"},{"start":134,"end":139,"surface":"brain","lemma":"brain","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"大脑"},{"start":140,"end":145,"surface":"waves","lemma":"wave","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"波"}],"phrases":[{"start":5,"end":17,"surface":"thousands of","gloss_zh":"成千上万的"},{"start":68,"end":87,"surface":"electrical activity","gloss_zh":"电活动"},{"start":125,"end":133,"surface":"known as","gloss_zh":"被称为"},{"start":134,"end":145,"surface":"brain waves","gloss_zh":"脑电波"}]}]},{"sentences":[{"id":"s4","text":"For nearly a century, neuroscientists have studied these patterns using electroencephalography, or EEG.","separator_after":" ","translation_zh":"近一个世纪以来，神经科学家一直利用脑电图（即EEG）来研究这些模式。","tokens":[{"start":0,"end":3,"surface":"For","lemma":"for","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"长达"},{"start":4,"end":10,"surface":"nearly","lemma":"nearly","pos":"副词","gloss_zh":"将近"},{"start":11,"end":12,"surface":"a","lemma":"a","pos":"冠词","gloss_zh":"一个"},{"start":13,"end":20,"surface":"century","lemma":"century","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"世纪"},{"start":22,"end":37,"surface":"neuroscientists","lemma":"neuroscientist","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"神经科学家"},{"start":38,"end":42,"surface":"have","lemma":"have","pos":"助动词","gloss_zh":"已经"},{"start":43,"end":50,"surface":"studied","lemma":"study","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"研究"},{"start":51,"end":56,"surface":"these","lemma":"these","pos":"限定词","gloss_zh":"这些"},{"start":57,"end":65,"surface":"patterns","lemma":"pattern","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"模式"},{"start":66,"end":71,"surface":"using","lemma":"use","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"使用"},{"start":72,"end":94,"surface":"electroencephalography","lemma":"electroencephalography","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"脑电图技术"},{"start":96,"end":98,"surface":"or","lemma":"or","pos":"连词","gloss_zh":"或称"},{"start":99,"end":102,"surface":"EEG","lemma":"EEG","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"脑电图"}],"phrases":[{"start":0,"end":20,"surface":"For nearly a century","gloss_zh":"近一个世纪以来"}]},{"id":"s5","text":"Traditional EEG systems require participants to wear a snug cap fitted with dozens of small metal sensors called electrodes.","separator_after":" ","translation_zh":"传统的EEG系统要求受试者佩戴一顶紧贴头皮的帽子，上面装配着几十个被称为电极的微型金属传感器。","tokens":[{"start":0,"end":11,"surface":"Traditional","lemma":"traditional","pos":"形容词","gloss_zh":"传统的"},{"start":12,"end":15,"surface":"EEG","lemma":"EEG","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"脑电图"},{"start":16,"end":23,"surface":"systems","lemma":"system","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"系统"},{"start":24,"end":31,"surface":"require","lemma":"require","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"要求"},{"start":32,"end":44,"surface":"participants","lemma":"participant","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"参与者"},{"start":45,"end":47,"surface":"to","lemma":"to","pos":"不定式标记","gloss_zh":"去"},{"start":48,"end":52,"surface":"wear","lemma":"wear","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"佩戴"},{"start":53,"end":54,"surface":"a","lemma":"a","pos":"冠词","gloss_zh":"一顶"},{"start":55,"end":59,"surface":"snug","lemma":"snug","pos":"形容词","gloss_zh":"紧贴的"},{"start":60,"end":63,"surface":"cap","lemma":"cap","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"帽子"},{"start":64,"end":70,"surface":"fitted","lemma":"fit","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"装配"},{"start":71,"end":75,"surface":"with","lemma":"with","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"带有"},{"start":76,"end":82,"surface":"dozens","lemma":"dozen","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"几十个"},{"start":83,"end":85,"surface":"of","lemma":"of","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"……的"},{"start":86,"end":91,"surface":"small","lemma":"small","pos":"形容词","gloss_zh":"小型的"},{"start":92,"end":97,"surface":"metal","lemma":"metal","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"金属"},{"start":98,"end":105,"surface":"sensors","lemma":"sensor","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"传感器"},{"start":106,"end":112,"surface":"called","lemma":"call","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"称为"},{"start":113,"end":123,"surface":"electrodes","lemma":"electrode","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"电极"}],"phrases":[{"start":64,"end":75,"surface":"fitted with","gloss_zh":"装配有；配备有"},{"start":76,"end":85,"surface":"dozens of","gloss_zh":"几十个；数十个"}]},{"id":"s6","text":"These sensors detect electrical signals passing through the scalp.","separator_after":" ","translation_zh":"这些传感器负责探测穿透头皮传出的微弱电信号。","tokens":[{"start":0,"end":5,"surface":"These","lemma":"these","pos":"限定词","gloss_zh":"这些"},{"start":6,"end":13,"surface":"sensors","lemma":"sensor","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"传感器"},{"start":14,"end":20,"surface":"detect","lemma":"detect","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"探测"},{"start":21,"end":31,"surface":"electrical","lemma":"electrical","pos":"形容词","gloss_zh":"电的"},{"start":32,"end":39,"surface":"signals","lemma":"signal","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"信号"},{"start":40,"end":47,"surface":"passing","lemma":"pass","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"穿过"},{"start":48,"end":55,"surface":"through","lemma":"through","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"通过"},{"start":56,"end":59,"surface":"the","lemma":"the","pos":"定冠词","gloss_zh":"这"},{"start":60,"end":65,"surface":"scalp","lemma":"scalp","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"头皮"}],"phrases":[{"start":21,"end":39,"surface":"electrical signals","gloss_zh":"电信号"},{"start":40,"end":55,"surface":"passing through","gloss_zh":"穿过；穿透"}]},{"id":"s7","text":"In laboratory experiments, researchers examine how brain waves shift between slow rhythms, like those seen during rest, and faster frequencies, which often appear during active problem-solving.","separator_after":" ","translation_zh":"在实验室研究中，研究人员会观察脑电波如何在缓慢节律（如休息时观察到的节律）与更快频率（常出现在积极解题时）之间切换。","tokens":[{"start":0,"end":2,"surface":"In","lemma":"in","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"在……中"},{"start":3,"end":13,"surface":"laboratory","lemma":"laboratory","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"实验室"},{"start":14,"end":25,"surface":"experiments","lemma":"experiment","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"实验"},{"start":27,"end":38,"surface":"researchers","lemma":"researcher","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"研究人员"},{"start":39,"end":46,"surface":"examine","lemma":"examine","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"检查；观察"},{"start":47,"end":50,"surface":"how","lemma":"how","pos":"副词","gloss_zh":"如何"},{"start":51,"end":56,"surface":"brain","lemma":"brain","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"大脑"},{"start":57,"end":62,"surface":"waves","lemma":"wave","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"电波"},{"start":63,"end":68,"surface":"shift","lemma":"shift","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"转换"},{"start":69,"end":76,"surface":"between","lemma":"between","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"在……之间"},{"start":77,"end":81,"surface":"slow","lemma":"slow","pos":"形容词","gloss_zh":"缓慢的"},{"start":82,"end":89,"surface":"rhythms","lemma":"rhythm","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"节律"},{"start":91,"end":95,"surface":"like","lemma":"like","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"像"},{"start":96,"end":101,"surface":"those","lemma":"those","pos":"代词","gloss_zh":"那些（节律）"},{"start":102,"end":106,"surface":"seen","lemma":"see","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"被观察到"},{"start":107,"end":113,"surface":"during","lemma":"during","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"在……期间"},{"start":114,"end":118,"surface":"rest","lemma":"rest","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"休息"},{"start":120,"end":123,"surface":"and","lemma":"and","pos":"连词","gloss_zh":"和"},{"start":124,"end":130,"surface":"faster","lemma":"fast","pos":"形容词比较级","gloss_zh":"更快的"},{"start":131,"end":142,"surface":"frequencies","lemma":"frequency","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"频率"},{"start":144,"end":149,"surface":"which","lemma":"which","pos":"关系代词","gloss_zh":"它们"},{"start":150,"end":155,"surface":"often","lemma":"often","pos":"副词","gloss_zh":"常常"},{"start":156,"end":162,"surface":"appear","lemma":"appear","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"出现"},{"start":163,"end":169,"surface":"during","lemma":"during","pos":"介词","gloss_zh":"在……期间"},{"start":170,"end":176,"surface":"active","lemma":"active","pos":"形容词","gloss_zh":"积极的"},{"start":177,"end":192,"surface":"problem-solving","lemma":"problem-solving","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"问题解决"}],"phrases":[{"start":3,"end":25,"surface":"laboratory experiments","gloss_zh":"实验室实验"},{"start":51,"end":62,"surface":"brain waves","gloss_zh":"脑电波"}]},{"id":"s8","text":"They also measure event-related potentials, or ERPs, which track the brain’s immediate electrical response to specific tasks, such as reading a word or resisting an impulse.","separator_after":"","translation_zh":"他们还会测量事件相关电位（ERPs），用以追踪大脑对特定任务（如阅读词语或克制冲动）的即时电反应。","tokens":[{"start":0,"end":4,"surface":"They","lemma":"they","pos":"代词","gloss_zh":"他们"},{"start":5,"end":9,"surface":"also","lemma":"also","pos":"副词","gloss_zh":"也"},{"start":10,"end":17,"surface":"measure","lemma":"measure","pos":"动词","gloss_zh":"测量"},{"start":18,"end":31,"surface":"event-related","lemma":"event-related","pos":"形容词","gloss_zh":"事件相关的"},{"start":32,"end":42,"surface":"potentials","lemma":"potential","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"电位"},{"start":44,"end":46,"surface":"or","lemma":"or","pos":"连词","gloss_zh":"或称"},{"start":47,"end":51,"surface":"ERPs","lemma":"ERP","pos":"名词","gloss_zh":"事件相关